"note": "Born in Texas, died in Ohio at 87; buried at Spring Grove Cemetery in Cincinnati. His Social Security record names his parents: Rannie Pullen and Eva L. West. He and Rose Marie appear together in the 1950 census in Campbell County, Kentucky. Sarah M. Pullen's 2011 obituary records 14 cousins among his grandchildren's generation — the combined children of his six surviving children (Stephen, Richard, Robert, Kenneth, Patricia, Margo, Lorianne). Most of them are living and not yet named in any public record. Named as Rose Marie's surviving husband in her 2012 obituary, which records 11 grandchildren and nine great-grandchildren at that date. A separate public member tree (\"Robert M. Pullen\", owner ibobalooba1, 1,090 people) independently carries this family — Willard's dates, parents (Rannie Pullen + Eva West), wife and children — and adds his 1948 Covington address (4332 Vermont Ave., \"lived at this address before married\") and later Milford / North College Hill, Ohio residences. Eight of the fourteen cousins of Sarah's 2011 obituary are now identified by record on this tree: Hillary Suzanne and Clarissa Marie Pullen (Richard's daughters); Kenneth Stephen and Sean Walter Pullen (Stephen's); Steven Christopher and Anthony David Pullen (Kenneth's); Kelly Elizabeth and Stacey Marie Piepmeier (Lorianne's). The remainder — including two unnamed children recorded for Stephen, one for Kenneth, and any children of Patricia or Margo — is untraced. NEEL-PICKREL 2026-10-15 (round 41): two Ohio records the hint engine attached to his mother Eva are his: the Ohio death record for “West”, female parent of “Willard Pullen”, filed 14 October 2005 (certificate 81784) matches his 27 September 2005 death, and the Spring Grove Cemetery index entry (spouse Rannie Pullen, child Willard Pullen) records the Cincinnati burial. Both name his mother's maiden name West. ROUND 63 (2026-10-17, potentials sweep): the cousin arithmetic settled and the index limit that blocks the rest. Nine of Sarah's fourteen cousins now stand named — the eight the birth records identify (Hillary Suzanne and Clarissa Marie Pullen; Kenneth Stephen and Sean Walter Pullen; Steven Christopher and Anthony David Pullen; Kelly Elizabeth and Stacey Marie Piepmeier) plus Michael Shane Pullen, named in Sarah's own 2011 obituary as her brother. The five still untraced are two of Stephen's four (per the member tree), one of Kenneth's three (the 1989 divorce records three minor children, two identified), and any child of Patricia's or Margo's. This round established WHY they stay untraced: the Ohio Birth Index cannot be searched by parent or by birth year at all. Its own form submits Mother First+Last as ?mother=First_Last and the index ignores it (the query returns the whole collection, 1,242,710 rows), and a birth-year filter returns 1,142,198 unfiltered rows; what does work is a Name search, a father-SURNAME filter (?father=_Pullen, 5,728 rows across 1908-2003, with no year narrowing available) and the Additional Information field — which is the mother's maiden name and is populated only for pre-1965 entries: ?f-Notes=Pullen returns exactly 72 records, every one dated 1909-1964, all read in full this round. A child of a Pullen daughter born 1972-1996 therefore cannot be reached through Ohio by its mother's maiden name, and the Kentucky index — which does key on the mother's maiden name — holds no Morrison, Young or Woods child of a Pullen mother in 1971-1999. The block is the indexes' own structure, not a missing query.",
