"note": "Uriah's father — another generation of the Hart line in Kentucky. PHOTO AUDIT 2026-10-14: removed a Find A Grave photo that belonged to a different person (FG memorial is uriah-hart (86538285) but person is Abraham Hart) — the memorial's own photo now sits on that person's card instead. The death-record index entry of a Joseph Hart names his father Abram Hart, born Virginia — a possible son of this Abraham (candidate, unconfirmed). REJECTED 2026-10-15: the 1938 city-directory hint attached to this card (Abr Hart, 2207 Loyola, wife Amelia) postdates this Abraham's 1847 death — a namesake; not used.\n\nROUND 60 (2026-10-16, potentials sweep): his marriage is now documented — the Kentucky County Marriage Records read \"Abraham Hart\" × \"Amelia Terry,\" 3 Feb 1817 (bond/return page; film 000390788) with the Compiled Marriages reading 2 Mar 1817, Hardin County; the U.S. and International Marriage Records add the birth places, Abraham b. 1797 in South Carolina and Amelia b. 1800 in Virginia. The \"Kentucky Soldiers of the War of 1812\" hint was read and set aside: this Abraham's 1797 birth is too late for the war, and the volume's index page carries only earlier Harts — recorded, not adopted.",
