"note": "Candidate (unconfirmed): the 1802 will of Robert Hinson of Fauquier Co., Virginia provides for an \"Elizabeth Whitten\" — probably this Elizabeth, who married John W. Whitten in Fauquier (1795); the abstract states no relationship. Robert's sons James and Tapley Hinson were executors. REJECTED 2026-10-15: the Essex and Northamptonshire records attached to this card name English Elizabeth Whittons of other families (Woodford, Essex — husband Jonathan; Helmdon/Tiffield, Northamptonshire — husband John); not used. CONFLICT (round 53): the 17 Jun 1795 Fauquier marriage record names the bride “Alice Ore” — this card's 1795 marriage reading is unconfirmed; both kept.\n\nROUND 60 (2026-10-16, potentials sweep): the will abstract behind this card has now been read from the volume's own page image — \"Abstracts of Fauquier County, Virginia,\" Will Book 3 (1796-1803), p. 355: \"HINSON, Robert — [will dated March 1802; the day digit reads as 23 or 29 in the scan], proved 26 April 1802. Elizabeth Whitten to receive $20 per month. Daughter, Ann Dials (or Dealls). All children not named. Exrs: James Hinson, Tapley Hinson (sons). Wit: John Blackwell, John Brough, Thomas Blackwell.\" The abstract states no relationship to Robert, so the parentage reading stays a candidate — but the bequest (an income for life to Elizabeth Whitten) and the executor sons are now quoted from the book itself.",
