"note": "Daughter of John and Jeanette Collins. Married Roy Gene Magee; lives in the Corinth / Williamstown area of Grant County. SWEEP 2026-10-15 (potentials round 37): the Kentucky birth index 1961-1999 files were scanned in full for her as mother: the only “Glenda Collins” mother-rows in the index are two Marshall County Thweatt children (1986, 1987) belonging to a different woman of the same name; nothing under this Glenda. The Kentucky marriage index 1973-1999 shows no Magee × Collins marriage.\n\nROUND 48 (2026-10-15): the marriage and obituary lanes were swept again for a record tying her to Roy Magee, and they came back negative. Kentucky marriage index 1973-1999, searched under her name: 193 fuzzy rows, the rows read (22) all carrying other grooms (Banks, Young, Hall, Harris, Thweatt, Pennington, Johnson, Wheeler) with no Grant County return, and no Magee or McGee groom anywhere in them. Ohio marriage abstracts (1970, 1972-2022), birth-narrowed to 1975-1980: 38 fuzzy rows under Glenda Collins and 8 under Glenda Magee, none of them a woman of either name (the matches are other given names); 16 more under the McGee spelling, likewise none. Ohio divorce abstracts, same band: 112 fuzzy rows, none a Glenda Magee. Newspapers.com obituary index under Glenda Magee: 4,908 fuzzy rows, the rows read all Mississippi, Louisiana or Virginia women. Recorded so no future round re-chases these lanes; the tribute-wall line remains the only evidence of the household.\n\nROUND 60 (2026-10-16, potentials sweep): the 2021 obituary's own survivors list — not just the tribute wall — names her: \"grandchildren, Kathy Emerson, Glenda Magee (Roy), Tonya Smith (Eddie), Amy Curtsinger, Bradley Emerson (Alsiha), Walter Newbury, Jeffery Newbury, Amanda Peyton (Garnett) and Renea Arnold\" (Evalee G. (Gilpin) Worthington Emerson obituary, Browning Funeral Home, May 2021). The obituary itself places her as Evalee's granddaughter; Austyn and Collin appear only in the tribute-wall signature — see their cards.",
