"mo": "mary-elizabeth-coffman",
"note": "Jordon Rousey's brother (Find A Grave #22575639). The U.S. and International Marriage Records carry “Leonard Rowsey, born 1818 in Kentucky” with wife Mary Ann Bibb, born 1823 in Kentucky, the marriage state recorded as Indiana — wired as a candidate (single source, no marriage year given).\n\nROUND 60 (2026-10-16, potentials sweep): his marriage is now documented, not just candidate — the Kentucky County Marriage Records read \"Leonard Rowsey\" × \"Mary Ann Bibb,\" 26 Mar 1840, Mercer County (film 000191857), and the U.S. and International Marriage Records agree (his birth 1818 in Kentucky, hers 1823, marriage state Indiana), so the couple is on record by name and date. His Civil War service came in with it: the Web: Indiana Civil War Soldier Database indexes \"Leonard Ronsey\" (the index's spelling), born about 1818, age 43, enrolled 22 Apr 1861 at Vernon, Indiana, discharged 15 May 1862, Company K, 12th Regiment, mustered out at Washington, DC, and the related records carry a Civil War pension index entry and a Union headstone (U.S., Headstones Provided for Deceased Union Civil War Veterans). A son is named by record: the Indiana Select Marriages Index entry for the marriage of Samuel J. Rousey records his parents as \"Leonard J. Rousey\" and \"Mary M. Bebb\" (the spelling there reads Bebb) — Samuel J. Rousey now has his own card. UNSETTLED: a 1922 Indiana death-certificate index entry filed as \"Nenard Rousey\" (roll 13) names spouse Mary E. Bibb and child Sarah Ellen Helmoth — the 1922 year does not fit this Leonard (Find A Grave reads d. 1881), so it is recorded as a next-generation lead, not merged.",
